  "description": "The Omnium CXC stands for Cyclo Cross City, and does just that. Commute, gravel, cyclocross, world tour, or alleycat – the CXC will work for you.\n\nWith 700x45c tire clearance and triple cage fork mounts, this thing is even adventure ready! Adjustable dropouts let you run singlespeed, fixed, Internal gear hub, or a derailleur. It’s now also belt drive compatible!\n\nWe could go on about possibilities, but in short the CXC is a true Swiss Army knife. There is nothing more versatile.\n\nThe Omnium CXC Titanium is the premium version of our classical CXC bike, improving it even further with a super-light titanium frame. All parts are carefully selected and designed for a perfect cycling experience.\n\nThe fork features a straight blade design, matte 3k carbon weave, 100x12mm thru axle, mudguard eyelets, and triple cage mounts!\n\nTitanium is unmatched: it won’t rust, crack, or corrode, no matter the conditions. It’s lighter than steel but just as tough, delivering a smooth, responsive ride with zero maintenance fuss. Simply put — steel is real, but titanium is realer.\n\nGetting the perfect fit makes all the difference in how your Omnium feels and performs. Use the chart to find the frame size that best matches your height.\n\nEach Omnium frame size covers a range of rider heights, so if you’re between sizes, consider how you like your bike to feel:\n\nWith On-Demand OMNIUM titanium frames are made to order and finished to your preference as a frame kit or complete, based on your wishes.\n\nChoose model, complete or frame kit, size, decal or anodizing, optional titanium and carbon parts and any accessories – Once the frame arrives it will be built up to your chosen specifications.\n\nWe open up orders for Titanium On-Demand 4 times a year and lead time starts when the on-demand window closes – See the on-demand order schedule for the next windows.\n\nFrame kits are quicker to build up and will start shipping first. All bikes are shipped within 2 weeks of arrival.\n\nThe order window for Titanium bikes will be open in the following periods\n\nGeometry is the same across steel and titanium but tubing is changed to add more stiffness to the titanium frame.",
